NAME
       tracepath - show the routers on the way to a host

SYNOPSIS
       tracepath [-n] HOST

DESCRIPTION
       tracepath lists each router (hop) that packets pass on their way to
       HOST, with the time each one took to answer and the largest packet
       size (MTU) of the path. It needs no root rights and is part of
       iputils, so it is installed even where traceroute is not. A line of
       "no reply" marks a hop that did not answer, often a firewall.

OPTIONS
       -n     Print addresses only; do not look up names.

EXAMPLES
           tracepath -n 192.168.50.254

SEE ALSO
       traceroute(8), ping(8), ip(8)
